{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls -l fullgame-network-test.py 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,100p' hub-test.py; cat gameplay-test-results.json | tail -15\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 11062 Nov  5 21:38 fullgame-network-test.py\n\"\"\"AI Hub harness checks for the bundled Demon Rumble HTML.\nRun with the installed Playwright Python. Owns and terminates only its own server.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom urllib.parse import urlencode\nfrom urllib.request import urlopen\n\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\n\nDEV = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nROOT = DEV.parent\nGAME = ROOT / f'{DEV.name}.html'\nSCENARIOS = [\n    ('two-player', {'players': 2}),\n    ('four-player-degraded', {'players': 4, 'latency': 150, 'jitter': 50, 'loss': 5}),\n    ('host-leave', {'players': 4, 'latency': 150, 'jitter': 50, 'loss': 5, 'scenario': 'host-leave'}),\n    ('dedicated-server', {'players': 2, 'scenario': 'server'}),\n]\n\n\ndef run(selected=None, fallback=False):\n    reports = []\n    failures = []\n    count = 0\n    server = subprocess.Popen(\n        [sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1', '--directory', str(ROOT)],\n        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n        stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n        text=True,\n    )\n    try:\n        line = server.stdout.readline()\n        port_match = re.search(r'port (\\d+)', line)\n        if not port_match:\n            raise RuntimeError(f'Loopback server failed to announce its port: {line.strip()}')\n        origin = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port_match.group(1)}'\n        with urlopen(f'{origin}/{GAME.name}', timeout=10) as response:\n            html = response.read().decode()\n        if '<title>Demon Rumble' not in html or 'hub:session-mode' not in html:\n            raise RuntimeError('The served HTML is not the bundled Demon Rumble game.')\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\n            browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True, args=[\n                '--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\n                '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required',\n            ])\n            try:\n                for name, parameters in SCENARIOS:\n                    if selected and name not in selected:\n                        continue\n                    context = browser.new_context(viewport={'width': 1440, 'height': 900})\n                    if fallback:\n                        context.add_init_script(\"Object.defineProperty(navigator,'gpu',{value:undefined,configurable:true});\")\n                    page = context.new_page()\n                    errors = []\n                    page.on('pageerror', lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n                    query = urlencode({'game': f'/{GAME.name}', 'auto': 1, 'limit': 12, 'play': 6000, **parameters})\n                    url = f'{origin}/{DEV.name}/hub-reference/harness.html?{query}'\n                    try:\n                        page.goto(url, wait_until='domcontentloaded', timeout=30000)\n                        page.wait_for_function(\"document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\", timeout=90000)\n                        report = page.evaluate('window.__hubCheck')\n                        report['scenarioName'] = name\n                        report['pageErrors'] = errors\n                        report['gameStates'] = []\n                        for frame in page.frames:\n                            if f'/{GAME.name}?' not in frame.url:\n                                continue\n                            state = frame.evaluate('window.__game?.state() ?? null')\n                            if state:\n                                report['gameStates'].append({key: state.get(key) for key in ['ready', 'backend', 'mode', 'wave', 'network']})\n                        for check in report.get('checks', []):\n                            count += 1\n                            if not check['pass']:\n                                failures.append(f\"{name}: {check['name']}: {check.get('detail', '')}\")\n                        count += 1\n                        if errors:\n                            failures.append(f\"{name}: page errors: {'; '.join(errors[:3])}\")\n                        count += 1\n                        if not report.get('gameStates'):\n                            failures.append(f'{name}: no live game state found')\n                        if report.get('pass') is not True and not any(name + ':' in failure for failure in failures):\n                            failures.append(f'{name}: harness did not pass')\n                        reports.append(report)\n                    except Exception as error:\n                        count += 1\n                        failures.append(f'{name}: {error}')\n                        reports.append({'scenarioName': name, 'pass': False, 'error': str(error), 'pageErrors': errors})\n                    finally:\n                        context.close()\n            finally:\n                browser.close()\n    finally:\n        server.terminate()\n        try:\n    \"mode\": \"victory\",\n    \"wave\": 7,\n    \"elapsed\": 86.66666666666303,\n    \"kills\": 162,\n    \"runStats\": {\n      \"splits\": 52,\n      \"dashes\": 15,\n      \"pulses\": 10,\n      \"pickups\": 19,\n      \"bossPhases\": 3\n    }\n  },\n  \"passed\": 39,\n  \"failed\": 0\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The revised demo AI has completed three campaigns and a full attract-mode campaign, with every mechanic exercised. Controller, touch, local co-op revival, developer sliders, and synthesized audio checks are passing. I’m running the final combined checks now, including two actual game pages exchanging online input and reaching the same victory screen."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='../exit-interview.json';x=json.load(open(p));x['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium WebGPU and WebGL 2 visual fallback; three scripted complete campaigns plus default attract campaign; emulated standard gamepad; phone touch; OfflineAudioContext; real two-page WebRTC; AI Hub 2/4-player, latency 150 ms, jitter 50 ms, loss 5%, host-leave and dedicated-server harness. Physical controller, listening and strict-NAT reachability unknown.'\nx['testingFeedback']=['11 issues caught through automated tests, visual checks and integration review, all corrected: menu repeat, autoplay aim, remote gamepad routing, remote mouse/touch routing, guest results, host replay, remote animation, paused remote input, title wrapping, touch prompts, saved settings labels.','2 classified as critical for the controller-first online experience: remote controller routing and missing guest results. No known remaining critical failures.','Repeated complete campaign playthroughs caught an intermittent autoplay aiming stall; the multiplayer harness verified authority, departures and network impairment.','The software WebGPU screenshot was blank; state assertions and WebGL 2 fallback screenshots provided useful verification instead.']\nx['engineFeedback']=['Three.js geometry, node materials and native AnimationMixer made procedural ink silhouettes and expressive wingbeats straightforward.','Initial autoplay aimed behind moving targets; predictive aim and regular pulses resolved it. Software WebGPU screenshots were blank in this headless environment.','The fixed-step arcade simulation, combat behaviors, controller-first menu/input system, synth score and authoritative network snapshots.','Coordinating asynchronous WebGPU rendering with fixed-step Rapier sensor contacts and replicated world state.','none','A built-in toon and outline pipeline with identical behavior across WebGPU and WebGL.']\nx['promptFeedback']=['The concrete controller-first philosophy, source-inspired mechanics, attract mode and explicit verification requirements.','Standalone multiplayer topology and expected campaign duration were unspecified; chose manual WebRTC plus AI Hub sessions.','Completing and verifying a cohesive six-encounter campaign, all input methods and shared-world multiplayer in a single HTML file.','Specify whether relay-backed internet connectivity is required and give a target campaign duration.']\nopen(p,'w').write(json.dumps(x,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\nbiome format --write main.js audio.js network.js build.mjs verify.mjs style.css\nnpm install --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts\nnode build.mjs\nnode verify.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Demon Rumble\n\nOpen the single HTML file one directory above this folder in a current browser. It contains the engine, physics WASM, geometry, animation, audio and AI Hub client; no CDN download is needed. WebGPU is preferred, with a WebGL 2 fallback. Sound starts after the first input.\n\nAn original front-facing arcade shooter inspired by Demon Attack (1982). Six encounters introduce splitting demons, diving offspring, elite crossfire, forkfire and repair pickups, then a three-phase boss. Hull repairs between nights, chaining kills increases score, and co-op wingmates revive while a partner survives. Leaving the title idle for ten seconds starts a looping AI demonstration.\n\n- Controller: stick/D-pad move, Cross/A fire, Circle/B dash, Square/X pulse, Options/Menu pause.\n- Keyboard: A/D or arrows move, Space fire, Shift dash, E pulse, Esc pause.\n- Mouse: move to steer, left click fire, right click pulse.\n- Local player two: second pad, or J/L move, I fire, O dash, U pulse.\n- Touch: drag to steer with automatic fire, second finger dash, contact Pulse button when ready.\n\nPause → Developer tools exposes live enemy tempo, projectile speed, player fire rate and damage sliders, plus invincibility, autopilot, clear wave, jump to boss, refill and reset. Settings include music (10% by default), effects/voices, PlayStation/Xbox glyphs and reduced motion.\n\nAI Hub sessions support shared-world co-op for one to four players, including a dedicated server seat. The bundled, unmodified session client is version 1.4.0. Direct two-player WebRTC is available through Online Co-op: host shares an invitation, guest shares an answer, host pastes that answer. No accounts or broker are needed. Restrictive NAT compatibility is unknown because no TURN relay is configured.\n\n## Development\n\nRuntime: Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3, native Web Audio/Gamepad/WebRTC APIs. All models and audio are procedural. Wingbeats and engine flames use AnimationMixer clips; gameplay uses a fixed 60 Hz Rapier sensor world. Host snapshots are sent 12 times per second. No engine changes were made.\n\nFrom this directory, \"'`npm ci --ignore-scripts` installs the pinned build dependencies; `npm run build` writes the root HTML. `main.js` contains scene/combat/UI, `audio.js` the synthesizer, `network.js` the session adapter, `shell.html` the screens and `style.css` the visual styling. `exit-interview.json` is beside the delivered HTML and is embedded into About/Credits by the build.\n\nRun all automated verification with one command:\n\n```\nnode verify.mjs\n```\n\nIt prints failures and one aggregate check count. It runs the real campaign, emulated controller/touch, local co-op, audio render, network protocol checks, two-page WebRTC and the AI Hub harness. Browsers and ephemeral loopback servers are closed after use. The test runner uses the machine'\"'s installed Playwright Python environment. \"'`*-results.json` preserve structured evidence. Screenshots were used only for visual layout; the headless software WebGPU canvas can be blank, so WebGL 2 was used for visual inspection.\n\nSource information and all testing, engine and prompt feedback are available in the in-game Credits and the root exit interview. Usage is added on import.\nEOF\nrg -n '\"'TODO|Pending|placeholder' --glob '\"'!node_modules/**'\"' --glob '\"'!hub-reference/**'\"' --glob '\"'!*-results.json'\"' --glob '\"'!package-lock.json'\"' .\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
